# Scope the knowledge graph to shipped source only: src/ and plugins/*/src/.
#
# graphify's ignore file is EXCLUDE-ONLY -- a "!" line cannot re-include a path
# (detect.py: "adding a .graphifyignore can only ever exclude MORE, never
# re-include"). So a whitelist is impossible and everything outside the two
# source trees is listed explicitly below.
#
# Why scope at all: unscoped extraction produced 36,315 nodes, which is above
# graphify's 5,000-node visualization limit, so graph.html degraded to an
# aggregated community view instead of a node-level map.

# --- other tools' index internals: never ingest these ---
graphify-out/
.zvec-grep/
.serena/
.codegraph/

# --- tests, fixtures, evals ---
tests/
evals/
**/tests/
**/test/
**/testing/
**/fixtures/
**/__fixtures__/
**/snapshots/
**/conftest.py
test_*.py
*_test.py
*_spec.py
conftest.py
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/

# --- examples, generated sites ---
# docs/ and contributor/ are deliberately NOT excluded: their prose is part of
# what the graph should answer questions about.
examples/
**/examples/
site/
dist/

# --- agent + repo tooling, not product code ---
.agents/
.claude/
.github/
.spec/
.kiro/
.omo/
.release/
.vscode/
skills/

# --- non-source file types anywhere ---
# NOTE: *.md is intentionally absent so docs/ and contributor/ prose is indexed.
# Markdown inside an excluded directory stays excluded -- the directory rule wins.
*.toml
*.lock
*.json
*.yml
*.yaml
*.cfg
*.ini
*.txt
*.sh
*.ps1
*.html
*.css
LICENSE
